spider-man's far from home hasn't yet  swung on to theater screens for most  fans to see but the long-awaited Spidey  sequel premiered in Hollywood for  industry insiders and critics On June 26  the following day Marvel lifted its  embargo on far from home reviews and  outlets wasted no time publishing  critics initial reactions as of noon  eastern on the day the embargo lifted  far from home shined bright with a 92  percent approval rating on Rotten  Tomatoes that's well above the threshold  needed for a certified fresh'  distinction for the most part critics  are gushing about spider-man far from  home particularly for its quote breezily  unpredictable blend of team bromance and  superhero action as Rotten Tomatoes  itself summarizes it reviewers also love  that far from home quote stylish Lee  sets the stage for the next era of the  MCU by introducing characters like Jake  Gyllenhaal's Mysterio Danielle souls men  of soul Z at the movies gave the film  4.5 stars out of five writing that it  deals with the Avengers end game fallout  in a way that only this film can and is  able to close the chapter on one book  while laying the foundation for another  GamesRadar critic Jordan Farley called  far from home another home run for the  MCU that puts Pete's responsibilities in  a post Ironman world front and center  during a rib-tickling summer romance  whatever you do don't skip the credits  writing for Mashable Alexis Ned noted  that the Spider Man sequel wonderfully  follows up Avengers endgame and paves  the way for Holland's Peter Parker to  play an even bigger role in the MCU as  phase 4 begins far from home doesn't  waste an iota of the goodwill Marvel has  earned in its previous offerings every  cheeky nod towards Peter's future in the  MCU feels genuine even though the next  phase is still shrouded in mystery  spider-man far from home does a  fantastic job of latching the door that  end game closed while opening a whole  new universe of possibilities for Marvel  like Farley meds how did the importance  of the post-credits scene the Raps  Alonso do rod a noted that far from home  is quote an entertaining example of what  we used to call a summer movie thanks to  its playful romance between Peter Parker  and MJ I'm messing with you  thank you you're welcome you look pretty  too as well as Aunt May and happy Hogan  do radhe adds that it has steaks that  are about personal growth rather than  intergalactic Armageddon and some  satisfying hero on villain throwdowns  David Crowe at den of geek brought up  director Sam Raimi's original spider-man  trilogy in his review of far from home  writing that the flick is accepting of  Rama's legacy and incorporate some of  that high-flying iconography instead of  running from it he also gave kudos to  Gyllenhaal whom he thought played  Mysterio with quote wide-eyed intensity  there's a part of me that wants me to  tell you just turn around run away from  all this and then there's another part  of me that knows what we're about to  fight at Forbes Scott Mendelssohn wrote  that far from home is a quote robust  improvement upon homecoming at the very  least the film presents a Peter Parker  who was relatively good at his job and  doesn't consistently screw up to the  point where you wish he'd hang up the  costume before he kills someone that was  my biggest gripe with homecoming as the  film's Peter has to learn to be a hero  worthy of the Avenger stick turned him  into an MCU variation on Curious George  far from home offers more of what worked  last time and less of what didn't not  everyone felt the same way though as a  common criticism of far from home is  that it isn't as sleek as homecoming  despite being entertaining in its own  right USA TODAY's Brian Truitt was one  such critic writing far from home has a  lot more boxes to check than homecoming  in terms of storytelling and while it's  always enjoyable the film feels  unfocused in parts everything changes  when a major turn happens of the story  exploding can't talk about it at all  variety and the last half takes on a  very meta vibe with some of the craziest  visuals Marvel has unleashed in a while  and a stellar understanding of what  Gyllenhaal can do so well on screen  spider-man far from home has pulled in  some sour reviews to go alongside the  stellar ones I'm sorry I'm sorry doesn't  I understand  I just want to be like you and I want  you to be better Todd McCarthy at The  Hollywood Reporter called the film bumpy  with quote hokey and ill-judged  special effects ill motivated and less  than awesome action set-pieces and a  villain that isn't compelling enough the  New York Post's Johnny Ola sinski said  that far from Holmes action and logic  quote fall short of its awesome  predecessor while Pamela Powell of real  honest reviews kept things simple when  she called the sequel quote just another  formulaic superhero film even so the  general consensus is that the flick is  impressively charming fun funny and  totally rad judge for yourselves when  Spiderman far from home hits theaters  July 2nd check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about your favorite superhero  films are coming soon subscribe to our  YouTube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

